<statement>
<p>
Fill in the missing pieces in the conversion of the decimal integer <m>\displaystyle{\left({49}\right)}_{{{10}}}</m> into its binary (base-2) representation.
</p>
<p>
49 = 2<asterisk/>(24) + <fillin characters="1" /></p>
<p>
24 = 2<asterisk/>(12) + <fillin characters="1" /></p>
<p>
12 = 2<asterisk/>(6) + <fillin characters="1" /></p>
<p>
6 = 2<asterisk/>(3) + <fillin characters="1" /></p>
<p>
3 = 2<asterisk/>(1) + <fillin characters="1" /></p>
<p>
1 = 2<asterisk/>(0) + <fillin characters="1" /></p>
<p>
The binary representation of <m>\displaystyle{\left({49}\right)}_{{{10}}}</m> is <m>\displaystyle{(}</m><fillin characters="1" /><m>\displaystyle{)}_{{{10}}}</m>

</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p><ul><li>1</li><li>0</li><li>0</li><li>0</li><li>1</li><li>1</li><li>110001</li></ul></p>
</solution>
